{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/speeches/the-united-kingdom-remains-committed-to-accelerating-progress-on-the-2030-agenda-and-the-sustainable-development-goals-uk-national-statement-at-the-hi","content_id":"4fca1a90-628b-40fd-a50a-0353e74c13a7","description":"Statement by Ambassador Kate Foster, UK Chargé d’Affaires to the UN, at the High-level Political Forum on Sustainable Development.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>The United Kingdom remains committed to accelerating progress on the 2030 Agenda and the Sustainable Development Goals, especially for those most in need. </p>\n\n<p>I will begin with SDG 17 on partnerships, a key theme of the recent Global Partnerships Conference co-hosted by the United Kingdom and South Africa together with British International Investment and the Children’s Investment Fund.</p>\n\n<p>At the Conference, we heard consistent calls for a more collaborative model of development. One where countries set the direction, where international partners align behind shared priorities, and where success is measured by outcomes. </p>\n\n<p>We need to back local leadership and strengthen domestic systems.  </p>\n\n<p>And we need to bring a broader coalition of partners on board, business, technology, civil society, and philanthropy, to unlock new finance, innovation, and impact.   </p>\n\n<p>For the UK, this is what our modern approach to development is about. About partnerships grounded in mutual respect and shared responsibility. </p>\n\n<p>We also welcome this year’s focus on SDG 7, access to affordable, reliable, sustainable energy for all. Despite progress, it remains off track. </p>\n\n<p>Global instability has increased energy, food, and fertiliser costs, and has underlined the importance of diversifying supply chains away from fossil fuels and towards renewable energy.</p>\n\n<p>Through the Global Clean Power Alliance, the UK is helping countries to unlock investment, develop national action plans, and address barriers to clean energy transitions. </p>\n\n<p>An £88 million extension to the Transforming Energy Access programme will expand access to reliable and sustainable energy for those most in need. </p>\n\n<p>To conclude, the 2030 Agenda remains our shared compass, providing a common framework for collective action. </p>\n\n<p>As we look ahead, development cooperation must become less fragmented and more responsive to country needs. </p>\n\n<p>That is why we need continued commitment to the Secretary-General’s UN80 reform initiative to make that delivery on the ground even more effective.</p>\n\n<p>We look forward to working with all partners as we prepare for next year’s SDG Summit and begin shaping a future development framework that builds on the achievements of the 2030 Agenda.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:35:19Z"}],"delivered_on":"2026-07-14T15:00:00+01:00","first_public_at":"2026-07-15T14:35:19.000+01:00","image":{"alt_text":"","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a578cce2cbe5d1c179a6572/hlpf_14_july.png"},"location":"United Nations, New York","political":true,"speech_type_explanation":"Transcript of the speech, exactly as it was delivered"},"document_type":"speech","first_published_at":"2026-07-15T14:35:19+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/speeches/the-united-kingdom-remains-committed-to-accelerating-progress-on-the-2030-agenda-and-the-sustainable-development-goals-uk-national-statement-at-the-hi","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/speeches/the-united-kingdom-remains-committed-to-accelerating-progress-on-the-2030-agenda-and-the-sustainable-development-goals-uk-national-statement-at-the-hi","base_path":"/government/speeches/the-united-kingdom-remains-committed-to-accelerating-progress-on-the-2030-agenda-and-the-sustainable-development-goals-uk-national-statement-at-the-hi","content_id":"4fca1a90-628b-40fd-a50a-0353e74c13a7","document_type":"speech","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-15T13:35:19Z","schema_name":"speech","title":"The United Kingdom remains committed to accelerating progress on the 2030 Agenda and the Sustainable Development Goals: UK national statement at the High-level Political Forum on Sustainable Development","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/the-united-kingdom-remains-committed-to-accelerating-progress-on-the-2030-agenda-and-the-sustainable-development-goals-uk-national-statement-at-the-hi","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1315","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","base_path":"/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","content_id":"f9fcf3fe-2751-4dca-97ca-becaeceb4b26","details":{"acronym":"FCDO","brand":"foreign-commonwealth-development-office","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de4e90e0710be0354d7/s960_fcdo-main-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de48fa8f5490aff83b4/s300_fcdo-main-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Foreign, Commonwealth<br/>&amp; Development Office"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_a